# ESF Companion Licensing

Copyright (c) 2026 Nathan Madrid

The ESF Companion repository contains two kinds of work, each released
under a separate license.

## Content (framework, documentation, templates, prompts, examples)

All non-code material in this repository, including but not limited to:

- Framework documentation (`docs/`, `README.md`, `WALKTHROUGH.md`,
  `GETTING_STARTED.md`, `START_HERE.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `WORKFLOW.md`,
  `CHANGELOG.md`, and other Markdown files at the repository root)
- Templates (`templates/`)
- Examples (`examples/`)
- Prompts (`prompts/`)
- Sample projects (`sample/`)
- Course materials (`courses/`)
- Skill definition files (any `SKILL.md` or reference Markdown inside
  `.claude/` and `platforms/`)

is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
License (CC BY 4.0). See `LICENSE-CONTENT` for the full text.

## Code (scripts, configuration, web assets)

All software in this repository, including but not limited to:

- Shell scripts (`install.sh`, `setup-repo.sh`, `test/**/*.sh`,
  `.claude/statusline-command.sh`, `.claude/hooks/*.sh`)
- GitHub Actions workflows and issue templates (`.github/`)
- Plugin manifests and configuration (`platforms/cowork/.claude-plugin/plugin.json`,
  `.claude/settings.local.json`, `.qwen/settings.json`)
- Landing page assets (`landing/`)

is licensed under the MIT License. See `LICENSE-CODE` for the full text.

## How to cite

For academic citation, see `CITATION.cff` in this repository.

## Questions

If you are unsure which license applies to a specific file, open an
issue or contact the maintainer. As a rule of thumb: if the file is
human-readable prose or pedagogical material, treat it as CC BY 4.0
content. If the file is executable, configuration, or web markup,
treat it as MIT-licensed code.
